public with sharing class LeadImportService {

    public class ImportResult {
        public Integer successCount;
        public List<Id> insertedIds;
        public Map<Integer, String> errorsByIndex;

        public ImportResult() {
            this.successCount = 0;
            this.insertedIds = new List<Id>();
            this.errorsByIndex = new Map<Integer, String>();
        }
    }

    public static LeadImportService.ImportResult importLeads(List<Lead> leads) {
        ImportResult result = new ImportResult();

        if (leads == null || leads.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        // Track which input indexes are candidates for DML (not duplicates).
        List<Integer> candidateIndexes = new List<Integer>();
        List<Lead> candidateLeads = new List<Lead>();

        // Track first-seen emails (trimmed, lower-cased).
        Set<String> seenEmails = new Set<String>();

        for (Integer i = 0; i < leads.size(); i++) {
            Lead ld = leads[i];

            if (ld == null) {
                // Nothing sensible to do with a null lead; skip it as a candidate.
                result.errorsByIndex.put(i, 'Lead is null');
                continue;
            }

            // Normalise email for duplicate detection.
            String rawEmail = ld.Email;
            String normalizedEmail = null;
            if (rawEmail != null && rawEmail.trim().length() > 0) {
                normalizedEmail = rawEmail.trim().toLowerCase();
            }

            if (normalizedEmail != null) {
                if (seenEmails.contains(normalizedEmail)) {
                    result.errorsByIndex.put(i, 'Duplicate email in import: ' + normalizedEmail);
                    continue;
                }
                seenEmails.add(normalizedEmail);
            }

            // Default LeadSource to Web when blank.
            if (String.isBlank(ld.LeadSource)) {
                ld.LeadSource = 'Web';
            }

            candidateIndexes.add(i);
            candidateLeads.add(ld);
        }

        if (candidateLeads.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        // Single DML statement, partial-success allowed.
        Database.SaveResult[] saveResults = Database.insert(candidateLeads, false);

        for (Integer j = 0; j < saveResults.size(); j++) {
            Database.SaveResult sr = saveResults[j];
            Integer inputIndex = candidateIndexes[j];

            if (sr.isSuccess()) {
                result.successCount++;
                result.insertedIds.add(sr.getId());
            } else {
                List<String> messages = new List<String>();
                for (Database.Error err : sr.getErrors()) {
                    messages.add(err.getMessage());
                }
                result.errorsByIndex.put(inputIndex, String.join(messages, '; '));
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

A few notes on the design decisions:

- **`insertedIds` in input order:** `candidateLeads`/`candidateIndexes` are built in input order, and `Database.insert` returns `SaveResult`s in the same order as the input list, so appending successful Ids as we iterate preserves input order.
- **Duplicate-before-insert semantics:** Duplicate detection runs entirely before DML, so a later lead with a repeated email is never sent to the database and gets the duplicate error even if the first lead ultimately fails to insert.
- **Single DML:** Exactly one `Database.insert(..., false)` call per invocation, keeping it bulk-safe and partial-success tolerant.
- **No throwing:** `Database.insert` with `allOrNone = false` collects per-row results rather than throwing; null/empty input short-circuits with fully-initialised (never-null) members.
- **Sharing:** `with sharing` respects the running user's sharing rules.
- I defensively handled a `null` element in the list so the method cannot NPE; valid leads still import.

