/**
 * Utility for retrieving the active values of any picklist (or multi-select
 * picklist) field, chosen at runtime.
 */
public with sharing class PicklistService {

    /**
     * Represents a single active picklist option.
     */
    public class Option {
        public String value;      // the API value
        public String label;      // the display label
        public Boolean isDefault; // true only for the field's default value

        public Option(String value, String label, Boolean isDefault) {
            this.value = value;
            this.label = label;
            this.isDefault = isDefault;
        }
    }

    /**
     * Custom exception thrown for any invalid input or lookup failure.
     */
    public class PicklistServiceException extends Exception {}

    /**
     * Returns the active values of the given picklist / multi-select picklist
     * field, in the order they are defined on the field. Inactive values are
     * excluded.
     *
     * @param objectApiName case-insensitive object API name (standard or custom)
     * @param fieldApiName  case-insensitive field API name (standard or custom)
     * @return list of active Options in defined order
     * @throws PicklistServiceException when a name is null/blank, the object or
     *         field does not exist, or the field is not a picklist type.
     */
    public static List<PicklistService.Option> activeOptions(String objectApiName, String fieldApiName) {
        if (String.isBlank(objectApiName)) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException('Object API name must not be null or blank.');
        }
        if (String.isBlank(fieldApiName)) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException('Field API name must not be null or blank.');
        }

        // Resolve the object type (case-insensitive).
        Schema.SObjectType sobjType = Schema.getGlobalDescribe().get(objectApiName.toLowerCase());
        if (sobjType == null) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException('Object does not exist: ' + objectApiName);
        }

        // Resolve the field (case-insensitive).
        Schema.DescribeSObjectResult objDescribe = sobjType.getDescribe();
        Schema.SObjectField field = objDescribe.fields.getMap().get(fieldApiName.toLowerCase());
        if (field == null) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException(
                'Field does not exist on ' + objDescribe.getName() + ': ' + fieldApiName
            );
        }

        // Validate that the field is a picklist or multi-select picklist.
        Schema.DescribeFieldResult fieldDescribe = field.getDescribe();
        Schema.DisplayType fieldType = fieldDescribe.getType();
        if (fieldType != Schema.DisplayType.PICKLIST && fieldType != Schema.DisplayType.MULTIPICKLIST) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException(
                'Field is not a picklist or multi-select picklist: '
                + objDescribe.getName() + '.' + fieldDescribe.getName()
            );
        }

        // Build the list of active options in defined order.
        // getPicklistValues() already excludes inactive values and preserves
        // the order defined on the field.
        List<PicklistService.Option> options = new List<PicklistService.Option>();
        for (Schema.PicklistEntry entry : fieldDescribe.getPicklistValues()) {
            if (entry.isActive()) {
                options.add(new PicklistService.Option(
                    entry.getValue(),
                    entry.getLabel(),
                    entry.isDefaultValue()
                ));
            }
        }

        return options;
    }
}
```

**Notes on the implementation:**

- **Case-insensitive lookups:** `Schema.getGlobalDescribe().get(...)` and `fields.getMap().get(...)` both key on lowercased API names, so `account`/`INDUSTRY` resolve correctly for standard and custom objects/fields.

- **Active values only & order:** `getPicklistValues()` returns entries in the order defined on the field; I additionally guard with `entry.isActive()` so inactive values (e.g. `Retired`) are excluded regardless of describe behavior.

- **Default detection:** `entry.isDefaultValue()` sets `isDefault` to `true` only for the field's configured default value.

- **Validation / exception safety:** Null/blank names, missing object, missing field, and non-picklist types each throw `PicklistServiceException`. Because I check for `null` returns from the describe maps before dereferencing, no `NullPointerException` leaks out.

- **Bulk-safe & governor-friendly:** The method performs no SOQL/DML; it uses only describe calls, so it's safe to call in loops and bulk contexts.

