public with sharing class AccountOnboardingService {

    public static List<Account> createAccountsWithContacts(Map<String, List<String>> contactLastNamesByAccountName) {
        List<Account> accounts = new List<Account>();

        if (contactLastNamesByAccountName == null || contactLastNamesByAccountName.isEmpty()) {
            return accounts;
        }

        fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork uow = new fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork(
            new List<Schema.SObjectType>{
                Account.SObjectType,
                Contact.SObjectType
            }
        );

        for (String accountName : contactLastNamesByAccountName.keySet()) {
            Account acct = new Account(Name = accountName);
            uow.registerNew(acct);
            accounts.add(acct);

            List<String> lastNames = contactLastNamesByAccountName.get(accountName);
            if (lastNames != null) {
                for (String lastName : lastNames) {
                    Contact con = new Contact(LastName = lastName);
                    // Register the contact as new, with its AccountId relationship
                    // resolved to the parent account's Id after insert.
                    uow.registerNew(con, Contact.AccountId, acct);
                }
            }
        }

        uow.commitWork();

        return accounts;
    }
}
```

The key requirement is that `Deal_Won__e` events must only be published *after* the opportunity updates are committed successfully. With fflib, registering platform events via `registerPublishAfterSuccessTransaction` ensures they only publish after the DML in the unit of work commits — matching "publish only after updates committed, and nothing published if save fails."

To register platform events in the unit of work, the UOW factory needs to be constructed with a publisher (e.g. `fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork.SendEmailWork` is for email; for events we need the UOW to support `registerPublishAfterSuccessTransaction`, which is available on `fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork` out of the box). The `Deal_Won__e` SObjectType must be included in the UOW's SObjectType list so the registration works, and since it's "Publish Immediately" we use `registerPublishAfterSuccessTransaction` so events only go out after the transaction's DML succeeds.

