public with sharing class AccountRatingService {

    // Threshold at which an open opportunity makes an account "Hot".
    @TestVisible
    private static final Decimal HOT_THRESHOLD = 100000;

    private static final String RATING_HOT  = 'Hot';
    private static final String RATING_WARM = 'Warm';
    private static final String RATING_COLD = 'Cold';

    /**
     * Asynchronously recalculates the Rating for each supplied Account based on
     * its open opportunity pipeline:
     *   - Hot  : at least one open opportunity with Amount >= 100,000
     *   - Warm : has open opportunities, but none that large
     *   - Cold : has no open opportunities
     *
     * Accepts a Set<Id> (required by @future) so a batch of opportunities results
     * in a single asynchronous call rather than one per record.
     */
    @future
    public static void recalculate(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Default every requested account to Cold; this is corrected below for
        // any account that still has open pipeline. Doing it this way guarantees
        // accounts whose last open opp just closed are set back to Cold.
        Map<Id, String> ratingByAccount = new Map<Id, String>();
        for (Id accId : accountIds) {
            ratingByAccount.put(accId, RATING_COLD);
        }

        // Scan the open opportunities for the affected accounts.
        for (Opportunity opp : [
                SELECT AccountId, Amount
                FROM Opportunity
                WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
                AND IsClosed = false
        ]) {
            Id accId = opp.AccountId;
            String current = ratingByAccount.get(accId);

            // Already Hot -> cannot be upgraded further.
            if (current == RATING_HOT) {
                continue;
            }

            if (opp.Amount != null && opp.Amount >= HOT_THRESHOLD) {
                ratingByAccount.put(accId, RATING_HOT);
            } else {
                // Has an open opp but not a big one -> at least Warm.
                ratingByAccount.put(accId, RATING_WARM);
            }
        }

        // Build the update list, only touching accounts whose Rating actually changes.
        List<Account> toUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Account acc : [
                SELECT Id, Rating
                FROM Account
                WHERE Id IN :accountIds
        ]) {
            String newRating = ratingByAccount.get(acc.Id);
            if (newRating != null && acc.Rating != newRating) {
                acc.Rating = newRating;
                toUpdate.add(acc);
            }
        }

        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update toUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

### A couple more notes
- **`with sharing`**: the service respects the running user's sharing. If your automation needs to rate accounts the triggering user can't see, switch to `without sharing` — but that's a deliberate security decision, so I left it as `with sharing` by default.
- **No-change short-circuit**: I only `update` accounts whose `Rating` actually differs, avoiding needless DML and recursive automation on Account.
- **`Amount` null-safety**: null amounts are treated as below the threshold, so they contribute `Warm`, not `Hot`.

